You now have a mine town altar with no guarding priest.
Maybe keep Jabby with you, maybe ditch him downstairs
and never return to that level.  But haul all of non-metalic
armor to the altar and BUC ID it.  Try on all items that are
not cursed.  Bingo much higher AC.

Note that by now you're seeing elves and dwarves in the
mines so you will likely fine mithril.  That's the best AC
to weight ratio other than dragon armor.  Think about the
trade off - Do you want to through daggers and depend
on your ravenous pet for protection for a while.

But you're also on a cleared out level of the mines.  The
watch will give you gloves, but it's also highly likely one
of the watch had studded leather armor.  Until getting
dragon armor that's the best for a spell casting offensive
wizard.  So there are your two body armor choices.
The watch also will probably give you either low or high
boots and they beat iron shoes for weight.

Since Jabby killed the priest there's a chance you have
a robe.  Hard trade off - [oMR vs robe.  If you eventually
get GDSM that is no longer a difficult trade off.  "oR,
DGSM, robe, plus whatever accessories you find are
one of the optimal combinations for a wizard.

